{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25600192",
      "title": "Redux Challenges & Introducing Redux Toolkit",
      "sourceHash": "a2912be1f885f5e40bb7a5fda05826806e426ba2b4352fa917304490694a9b06",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.29,
          "end": 4.23,
          "en": "So by now we learned a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.23,
          "end": 9.01,
          "en": "about the important basics of Redux and how we use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.01,
          "end": 12.562,
          "en": "Now the more complex our projects become",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.562,
          "end": 17.46,
          "en": "the more complex it can get to use Redux correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.46,
          "end": 19.41,
          "en": "Now the good thing is that in this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.41,
          "end": 22.68,
          "en": "you will of course see many examples also bigger projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.68,
          "end": 25.46,
          "en": "than this one but another good news",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.46,
          "end": 28.95,
          "en": "is that there is a slightly easier way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.95,
          "end": 31.22,
          "en": "of using Redux as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.22,
          "end": 35.16,
          "en": "Now I wanted to show you the core foundation first",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.16,
          "end": 37.26,
          "en": "so that you understand how it works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.26,
          "end": 39.76,
          "en": "but now I want to dive into an approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.76,
          "end": 43.28,
          "en": "that's a bit easier to set up and maintain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.28,
          "end": 46.006,
          "en": "Before we do that though, let's identify a couple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.006,
          "end": 49.4,
          "en": "of potential problems we could be facing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.4,
          "end": 52.54,
          "en": "if our application would continue to grow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.54,
          "end": 57.06,
          "en": "So if we manage more and more state with Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.06,
          "end": 60.93,
          "en": "One potential issue can be our action types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.93,
          "end": 64.55,
          "en": "These identifiers, I mentioned it before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.55,
          "end": 67.53,
          "en": "you of course have to avoid typos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.53,
          "end": 70.61,
          "en": "If you dispatch an action, you have to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.61,
          "end": 74.22,
          "en": "that you don't mistype the identifier here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.22,
          "end": 77.73,
          "en": "otherwise it of course won't be handled by the reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.73,
          "end": 80.46000000000001,
          "en": "or won't be handled correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.46000000000001,
          "end": 83.76,
          "en": "Now that's not a problem in a small app like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.76,
          "end": 87.35,
          "en": "but in bigger applications with a lot of developers working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.35,
          "end": 90.1,
          "en": "on the app and with a lot of different actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.1,
          "end": 91.66,
          "en": "it's super easy to imagine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.66,
          "end": 94.25,
          "en": "that you could mess up one of these identifiers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.25,
          "end": 97.61,
          "en": "You could even have clashing identifiers there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.61,
          "end": 100.06,
          "en": "so clashing identifier names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.06,
          "end": 102.18,
          "en": "So therefore having some way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.18,
          "end": 105.25,
          "en": "of defining those identifiers once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.25,
          "end": 108.37,
          "en": "and then reusing them would be nice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.37,
          "end": 110.91,
          "en": "And that is something we can do with JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.91,
          "end": 114.03999999999999,
          "en": "and something I will come back to in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.03999999999999,
          "end": 117.00999999999999,
          "en": "Another potential problem is the amount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.00999999999999,
          "end": 119.13,
          "en": "of data which we manage here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.13,
          "end": 122.34,
          "en": "The more data we have the more different pieces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.34,
          "end": 127.02,
          "en": "of state we have, the bigger our state objects get.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.02,
          "end": 130.33,
          "en": "And that means that we need to copy a lot of state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.33,
          "end": 133.23,
          "en": "when we update the counter we still need to copy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.23,
          "end": 136.78,
          "en": "and keep all the other state properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.78,
          "end": 140.05,
          "en": "and it also means that this reducer function gets longer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.05,
          "end": 142.04,
          "en": "and longer and all of a sudden",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.04,
          "end": 146.09,
          "en": "we might have an unmaintainable big Redux file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.09,
          "end": 149.57999999999998,
          "en": "And you might recall that I brought this up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.57999999999998,
          "end": 153.86,
          "en": "as one potential disadvantage of React Context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.86,
          "end": 157.8,
          "en": "If we put everything into one context provider file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 157.8,
          "end": 160.9,
          "en": "Now we can end up with the same problem with the Redux",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 160.9,
          "end": 164.503,
          "en": "but thankfully there are solutions for that with Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.493,
          "end": 168.55,
          "en": "Another potential problem we could be facing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 168.55,
          "end": 173.48,
          "en": "is the state immutability which we have to respect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 173.48,
          "end": 175.61,
          "en": "I talked about it in the last lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.61,
          "end": 177.53,
          "en": "We have to ensure that we always return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 177.53,
          "end": 179.55,
          "en": "a brand new state snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 179.55,
          "end": 181.78,
          "en": "and that we don't accidentally change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.78,
          "end": 183.83,
          "en": "the existing state anywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.83,
          "end": 186.73,
          "en": "And especially if you have more complex data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.73,
          "end": 190.55,
          "en": "with nested objects and arrays it's easy to mess this up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 190.55,
          "end": 192.97,
          "en": "and accidentally change some nested data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.97,
          "end": 195.3,
          "en": "even though you didn't want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 195.3,
          "end": 196.79,
          "en": "So it would be great if we would have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 196.79,
          "end": 198.69,
          "en": "some help with that as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 198.69,
          "end": 200.99,
          "en": "And if we could ensure that we don't accidentally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 200.99,
          "end": 205.01,
          "en": "manipulate nested data or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 205.01,
          "end": 208.22,
          "en": "Now for all those problems there are solutions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 208.22,
          "end": 210.05,
          "en": "we could implement on our own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 210.05,
          "end": 213.96,
          "en": "For example, for ensuring that we have unique identifiers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 213.96,
          "end": 217.74,
          "en": "and we don't miss type we could create constants,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.74,
          "end": 219.75,
          "en": "let's say a constant named increments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 219.75,
          "end": 222.15,
          "en": "which stores this identifier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 222.15,
          "end": 224.42000000000002,
          "en": "and we then export this constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 224.42000000000002,
          "end": 229.11,
          "en": "and we check that constants value here and we then import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 229.11,
          "end": 232.01,
          "en": "and use that constant in the counter component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 232.01,
          "end": 236.13,
          "en": "so that here we use the type increment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 236.13,
          "end": 238.85,
          "en": "and we just import increments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 238.85,
          "end": 243.85,
          "en": "So we import increment from going up store index.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 246.8,
          "end": 250.22,
          "en": "That is something we could do to fix this issue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 250.22,
          "end": 253.26,
          "en": "And these are approaches which we typically used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 253.26,
          "end": 256.03,
          "en": "in the past with Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 256.03,
          "end": 259.72,
          "en": "There also are solutions for splitting your reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 259.72,
          "end": 262.37,
          "en": "into multiple smaller reducers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 262.37,
          "end": 266,
          "en": "so that you don't get this large super big file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 266,
          "end": 269.95,
          "en": "and there also our solutions and third-party packages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 269.95,
          "end": 273.47,
          "en": "which allow you to automatically copy state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 273.47,
          "end": 276.39300000000003,
          "en": "and ensure that you don't accidentally edit it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 277.23,
          "end": 279.29,
          "en": "But we actually don't need to dive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 279.29,
          "end": 282.46,
          "en": "into those various solutions anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 282.46,
          "end": 286.9,
          "en": "Instead there is another library called Redux Toolkit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 286.9,
          "end": 288.94,
          "en": "And you can just Google for Redux Toolkit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 288.94,
          "end": 291.04,
          "en": "to find its official page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 291.04,
          "end": 294.27,
          "en": "It's actually developed by the same person",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 294.27,
          "end": 298.48,
          "en": "or the same team as React Redux and Redux itself",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 298.48,
          "end": 301.66,
          "en": "and Redux Toolkit simply as an extra package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 301.66,
          "end": 306.66,
          "en": "which makes working with Redux more convenient and easier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 306.83,
          "end": 310.86,
          "en": "You don't have to use it, unlike Redux and react Redux",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 310.86,
          "end": 313.84,
          "en": "which we installed before, you don't have to install",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 313.84,
          "end": 316.86,
          "en": "and use Redux toolkit but if you use it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 316.86,
          "end": 319.63,
          "en": "certain things will get easier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 319.63,
          "end": 322.26,
          "en": "And therefore, in the next lecture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 322.26,
          "end": 325.133,
          "en": "we're going to get started with Redux Toolkit.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}